Key design decisions:
- Comparison conditions: QuaRot (full pipeline incl. Hadamard), QuaRot-minus-Hadamard ablation (same calibration/PTQ algorithm and everything else, rotation matrix replaced by identity), RTN, GPTQ. Note QuaRot is not itself a rounding algorithm — in weight-only mode it's rotation + a quantizer (RTN or GPTQ). So the honest factorial design is 2 (rotate: identity vs Hadamard) × 2 (quantizer: RTN, GPTQ) = 4 cells, which naturally yields "QuaRot w/o Hadamard" = RTN/GPTQ baseline. Wait — careful: QuaRot rotation for weight-only requires folding H into weights: W' = H W (with X = X' H^T rotation invariance for RMSNorm-based layers, and the down_proj needing extra H). Actually in weight-only mode, QuaRot's rotation is equivalent to multiplying weights by Hadamard; then quantize W'. So the ablation "QuaRot minus Hadamard" = identity rotation with the same quantizer = plain RTN/GPTQ (up to any additional processing like scaling/equalization, which QuaRot doesn't add). So the control is nearly free but must be verified: e.g., perplexity of the identity-rotation GPTQ must match the plain GPTQ baseline numerically — a consistency check that validates the implementation.

Important subtlety: rotation-invariance equivalence requires that the rotation be applied consistently to both activations and weights (X W^T = (X H)(H^T W^T)); in weight-only mode, downstream layers' weights must be rotated too, so the equivalence holds only up to the quantization of the rotated weights. Also, fused layers need block-wise Hadamards. Also, the "extra" Hadamard for down_proj (H_{d_ff}) which cannot be folded into weights without breaking invariance — QuaRot handles down_proj by an extra pair of Hadamards (online, cheap). For weight-only, W_down can be rotated by H_1 on the input side, but that requires rotating the activations of up/gate projections accordingly. Hmm, details: In QuaRot, for weight-only quantization, the extra Hadamard matrices H1, H2 applied to down_proj input... Actually QuaRot applies an extra Hadamard H_1 to the input of down_proj; this changes the effective weight to W_down H_1^T, which is folded into the weight, and it's rotation-invariant because the previous operation is elementwise multiplication of two rotated quantities... In any case — the key point for the design: whether "QuaRot" includes the full invariance-preserving transform chain or just a left-multiplication of weights by Hadamard. This is one of the consequential assumptions the researcher raised.

Metrics:
- Primary: perplexity on WikiText-2 (or C4) with a fixed context length and sequence-packing strategy; report ΔPPL relative to FP16 baseline: ΔPPL = PPL_q - PPL_fp16, and relative degradation ΔPPL/PPL_fp16.
